
###
# Running Inferelator (snakemake htcondor profile)
###
# To run the script, we first need to ensure that all input files have been generated before condor-specific rules.
# that is, first comment out all things except part 0 under the rule all's input. Ensure that paths in config.yml are correct.
# Then run locally on a server that is not a condor submit node, with snakemake --cores 20 --use-conda -k --rerun-incomplete
# After generating all the required input, on a submit node, uncomment inferelator part of Part I below, and run (if too many jobs you may consider --batch all=1/3)
# snakemake --profile htcondor --use-conda -k --rerun-incomplete -np
# if the above does not produce something strange, do (you may consider --batch if too many jobs):
# snakemake --profile htcondor --use-conda -k --rerun-incomplete
# now, after all condor jobs have been completed, uncomment the Part 2 below for stability selection and analysis (from Inferelator starts to Inferelator ends).
# on a server different from the submit node, execute the command line: snakemake --cores 20 --use-conda -k --rerun-incomplete

###
# Running merlin (condor submit file)
###
# As the current snakemake profile does not supprot flocking, we use the condor submit files instead. Uncomment part 0 and part 0 only below 
# to generate required merlin inputs. Then after ("bash make_queue_args.sh", "condor_submit submit_files/submit_merlinp_p-5_r4.sub") generating
# all required condor output files, and organizing the outputs ("bash organize_merlin_condor_output.sh"), uncomment only the merlin part of Part 2
# under the rule all's input directive, and run 
# snakemake --cores 20 --use-conda -k --rerun-incomplete

###
# Running scMTNI (condor submit file)
###
# To run, comment out everything under "rule all, input:" except the line rules.scMTNI_with_TFA_input.input
# then snakemake --cores 20 --use-conda to generate scMTNI input. Then, submit to the condor by, e.g. (for FBS)
#
# mkdir -p GRN_outputs/algos/scMTNI/ibpg_2fct/processed_FBS_reprogramming/4_1
# num_ogids=$(ls ../real_dat_validation/scMTNI_data/scMTNI_sourcedata/processed_FBS_reprogramming/inputdata/scMTNI/data/ibpg_2fct/ogids/ | wc -l)
# for subsamp in {0..49}; do for og in $(seq 0 $((num_ogids - 1))); do echo ibpg_2fct randseed${subsamp} ${og}; done; done > scMTNI_queue_args/FBS_reprogramming.txt
# condor_submit submit_files/scMTNI_b-4_q1/processed_FBS_reprogramming.sub
#
# After all output files specified in submit_files/scMTNI_b-4_q1/processed_FBS_reprogramming.sub are there,
# comment out everything except rules.scMTNI_with_TFA_output.input and then run. Please check scMTNI specifics below before proceed.


